From: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 13:00:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] hwmon: ina2xx: Add INA234 support as INA226 variant

Add support for the Texas Instruments INA234 power monitor.

The INA234 is a 12-bit device with similar register layout to INA226.
The key difference is the bus voltage LSB: INA234 uses 3.125mV which
becomes 1.6mV effective LSB due to the 12-bit format (data in bits
[15:4] with bits [3:0] reserved).

Since 6.18 the driver selects alert and limit behaviour from a has_alerts
flag in the per-chip config rather than comparing against ina226 at each
site, so the six chip comparisons this used to add collapse into one flag.
Only hwmon_chip_update_interval still tests the id directly, and INA234
belongs there because it shares the INA226 CONFIG register layout.

Datasheet: https://www.ti.com/product/ina234

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [embedded specific]
Signed-off-by: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
---
 drivers/hwmon/ina2xx.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/hwmon/ina2xx.c b/drivers/hwmon/ina2xx.c
index bc3c1f7314b3..aa7f92ac5818 100644
--- a/drivers/hwmon/ina2xx.c
+++ b/drivers/hwmon/ina2xx.c
@@ -135,7 +135,7 @@ static const struct regmap_config ina2xx_regmap_config = {
 	.writeable_reg = ina2xx_writeable_reg,
 };
 
-enum ina2xx_ids { ina219, ina226, ina260, sy24655 };
+enum ina2xx_ids { ina219, ina226, ina260, sy24655, ina234 };
 
 struct ina2xx_config {
 	u16 config_default;
@@ -205,6 +205,17 @@ static const struct ina2xx_config ina2xx_config[] = {
 		.has_ishunt = false,
 		.has_power_average = true,
 	},
+	[ina234] = {
+		.config_default = INA226_CONFIG_DEFAULT,
+		.calibration_value = 2048,
+		.shunt_div = 400,
+		.bus_voltage_shift = 4,
+		.bus_voltage_lsb = 25600,
+		.power_lsb_factor = 32,
+		.has_alerts = true,
+		.has_ishunt = false,
+		.has_power_average = false,
+	},
 };
 
 /*
@@ -775,7 +786,7 @@ static umode_t ina2xx_is_visible(const void *_data, enum hwmon_sensor_types type
 	case hwmon_chip:
 		switch (attr) {
 		case hwmon_chip_update_interval:
-			if (chip == ina226 || chip == ina260)
+			if (chip == ina226 || chip == ina260 || chip == ina234)
 				return 0644;
 			break;
 		default:
@@ -990,6 +1001,7 @@ static const struct i2c_device_id ina2xx_id[] = {
 	{ "ina226", ina226 },
 	{ "ina230", ina226 },
 	{ "ina231", ina226 },
+	{ "ina234", ina234 },
 	{ "ina260", ina260 },
 	{ "sy24655", sy24655 },
 	{ }
@@ -1021,6 +1033,10 @@ static const struct of_device_id __maybe_unused ina2xx_of_match[] = {
 		.compatible = "ti,ina231",
 		.data = (void *)ina226
 	},
+	{
+		.compatible = "ti,ina234",
+		.data = (void *)ina234
+	},
 	{
 		.compatible = "ti,ina260",
 		.data = (void *)ina260
-- 
